==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*skrīþaną}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{m|ine-pro|*(s)kreyt-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*(s)ker-||twist, turn, bend}}. Germanic cognates include Old Saxon {{m|osx|skrīthan}}, Middle Dutch {{m|dum|schriden}} (Dutch {{m|nl|schrijden}}), Old High German {{m|goh|skrītan}} (German {{m|de|schreiten}}), Old Norse {{m|non|skríða}} (Swedish {{m|sv|skrida}}). The Indo-European root also gave Latin {{m|la|crīsō|crīsāre}} and Middle Irish {{m|mga|crith}} (Breton {{m|br|skrija||tremble with fear}}).

===Pronunciation===
